url: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302"
abstract: >-
  Version 0.2.0-preprint is a preliminary, unrefereed corrected snapshot of
  two-sided partial progress on Erdős Problem 302: a qualitative Lean-checked
  lower improvement over density 5/8 and the upper bound
  140803024/163562355. It is not independently verified or peer reviewed and
  is not a solution of Problem 302. The finite semantics, all exact packing
  certificates, omission argument, and upper asymptotic endpoint are connected
  by a source-closed Lean 4 development and cross-checked by exact
  dependency-free software. Here source-closed means that every project module
  has committed source, not that CI performs a cache-free rebuild. The theorem
  closure imports 80,127 modules from a SHA-256-verified .olean overlay. CI
  recompiles 48 modules in that closure, fresh-kernel-replays the imported
  environment through the integration module, and separately replays the final
  module while still structurally trusting .olean serialization. The
  lower theorem is Lean-checked through pinned
  external formal developments. AI systems assisted with search, code,
  formalization, and audits; the named author remains responsible for all
  claims. Software and verification material are MIT-licensed; the manuscript
  is CC BY 4.0 under the path-specific scope in LICENSE_SCOPE.md. Zenodo
  automatically archives the tagged source after the GitHub release; the
  complete verified release assets remain attached to the GitHub Release.
